test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T16:58:29.3361762Z             "body": "This draft preserves the original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging, lifecycle controls and fork-specific installation. Publishing remains disabled. It is not release-ready.\n\nLatest candidate: 74497b1. Revalidates SQLite version/project/key identity under the existing schema write lock, preventing three reproduced second-connection races from silently accepting a future/cleared schema version or missing project marker. Adds CI bootstrap phase notices, corrects Ubuntu mirror+file indirection, and collects independent ffmpeg frame-zero/pixel-grid diagnostics plus three isolated fresh macOS controls after an actual Chromium mismatch. Original files, strict assertions, action/RPC/job limits and default transports remain intact.\n\nValidation: 41 real journal/controller regressions each Node22/24; fresh installed production-package smoke passes; typecheck passes; first-frame diagnostics calibrated on Node20/22/24; three fresh controls preserve two existing recordings exactly; four receipt-gate and five mirror-shell cases pass; Bash syntax and actionlint pass (shellcheck/pyflakes disabled). PowerShell changes await native execution. Dry package:297 files, excludes QA fixtures/evidence.\n\nLatest completed native90 (58edfce): [batch](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39803246586) 1403 pass/6 fail; [original](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39803246848)578/3; completed summaries1981/9. Node20 main/package unexecuted after30m dependency-install cancellation. Four package steps pass. All17 job logs nonempty first read. Mac main207/4 recovered. Actual Codex1k passes on all three OS (36.145/39.741/79.104s, model0/owned0), without clearing native89 Windows CRASHED750 or historical ownership uncertainty.\n\nRemaining native90 failures: Mac raw/SDK/sync/retry timeouts; Windows privacy timeout before request classification; Windows component normal reopen rpc_timeout/init, last phase schema_commit, worker exit confirmed; original Mac Chromium gray first frame and Windows WebKit WAV/VP9 readiness. Mac WebKit producer, all12 trace and12 PDF behavior cases pass. Independent decoder diagnostics are prospective, not a producer fix. Full logs, snapshots and exact scopes are in docs/evidence/native90-summary.json and leading reports.\n\nCorrection: old mirror-step success and native89 fast setup did not prove a URI change. Native90 still used Azure via apt-mirrors.txt. The candidate now handles that indirection while preserving signing/security fallback; native performance remains unverified. Batch aggregate cancellation was requested only after all13 jobs were terminal; no running test was cancelled by that request.\n\nG00–G18 remain authoritative in docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md. No merge, publication, unsafe replay, ownership-debt clearance or full-matrix claim.",
